sizes for k = 0..11: 7, 15, 31, 63, 127, 255, 511, 1023, 2047, 4095, 8191, 16383  (size = 2^(k+3) - 1: True)
cost per round = 12.206 nats; so -ln P_T(phi_k) <= 12.77 + 12.206 k, while l_min(phi_k) >= 2^(k+3) - 1.
For every kappa > 0 and constant C, kappa * l_min(phi_k) - ln C exceeds -ln P_T(phi_k) for large k: Prop 6.9 fails; L1's code length is at most O(log) of derivation symbol size on this family.
